RAQL v0.1 Rust API sketch (types-first)

This is a concrete shape sketch for the Rust types and modules implied by
language_plan.md. The code blocks are sketches, not drop-in code.

---

1) raql-ir module layout

Suggested layout:

raql-ir/
  src/
    lib.rs
    source.rs          // RaqlFileId, SourceFile, SrcSpan
    symbol.rs          // Symbol helpers (intern::Symbol)
    ty.rs              // TyId, TyData, TypeInterner, TypeTag cache
    ast.rs             // Program<AstPhase>, directives, decls, TermAst, GoalAst
    resolved.rs        // Program<ResolvedPhase>, resolved atoms, enum ids
    typed.rs           // Program<TypedPhase>, VarId allocation, TermTyped
    planned.rs         // Program<PlannedPhase>, RulePlan, OpPlan, strata, SCCs
    diag.rs            // Diagnostic structs (phase-agnostic)

Phase-typed program container:

pub mod phase {
    pub trait Phase: sealed::Sealed {}
    pub struct AstPhase { pub items: Vec<AstItem> }
    pub struct ResolvedPhase { pub items: Vec<ResolvedItem> }
    pub struct TypedPhase { pub rules: la_arena::Arena<TypedRule> }
    pub struct PlannedPhase { pub strata: Box<[StratumPlan]> }
}

pub struct Program<P: phase::Phase> {
    pub common: ProgramCommon,
    pub phase: P,
}

pub struct ProgramCommon {
    pub sources: SourceMap,
    pub pragmas: Pragmas,
    pub types: TypeTable,
    pub preds: PredTable,
}

---

2) IDs and arenas

Use la_arena::Arena<T> with typed IDs everywhere.

pub type PredId = la_arena::Idx<PredDef>;
pub struct PredDef { pub sig: PredSig, pub src: SrcSpan }

pub type EnumId = la_arena::Idx<EnumDef>;
pub struct EnumDef {
    pub name: Symbol,
    pub variants: Box<[VariantId]>,
}

pub type VariantId = la_arena::Idx<VariantDef>;
pub struct VariantDef { pub name: Symbol, pub ordinal: u32 }

---

3) Types: interned TyId graph + canonical TypeTag

pub struct TyId(la_arena::Idx<TyData>);

enum TyData {
    Int,
    String,
    Bool,
    Opaque(OpaqueTy),
    Enum(EnumId),
    Option(TyId),
    List(TyId),
}

pub enum OpaqueTy { Def, Span, TypeRef, Node, Call, Ref, Impl, Path }

TypeTag is a cached canonical string, used by stable_order:

int, string, bool
option<T>, list<T>
RenderMode
Def, Span, TypeRef, Node, Call, Ref, Impl, Path

---

4) Terms: AST vs typed vs runtime

AST term:

pub enum TermAst {
    Var(Symbol),
    Wildcard,
    Int(i64),
    Str(Symbol),
    Bool(bool),
    EnumAtom { enm: Symbol, var: Symbol },
    None { ann: Option<TypeAst> },
    Some(Box<TermAst>),
    List { elems: Vec<TermAst>, ann: Option<TypeAst> },
}

Typed term:

pub struct TermTyped {
    pub ty: TyId,
    pub kind: TermKindTyped,
}

pub enum TermKindTyped {
    Var(VarId),
    Wildcard,
    Int(i64),
    Str(Symbol),
    Bool(bool),
    Enum { enum_id: EnumId, variant: VariantId },
    None,
    Some(Box<TermTyped>),
    List(Vec<TermTyped>),
}

Runtime term graph (unification + occurs check):

pub enum RTerm<H: HostTypes> {
    Var(VarId),
    Value(Value<H>),
    Some(TermId),
    None(TyId),
    List(Box<[TermId]>),
}

---

5) Predicate signatures and modes

pub enum PredKind { Rel, Func }

bitflags::bitflags! {
    pub struct PredAttr: u8 {
        const EXTERN = 0b0001;
        const INPUT  = 0b0010;
        const OUTPUT = 0b0100;
    }
}

pub struct PredSig {
    pub name: Symbol,
    pub arity: u32,
    pub args: Box<[TyId]>,
    pub kind: PredKind,
    pub attr: PredAttr,
}

pub struct ModeSig {
    pub pred: PredId,
    pub args: Box<[ModeArg]>,
}

pub struct ModeArg {
    pub dir: ModeDir,
    pub ty: TyId,
}

pub enum ModeDir { In, Out }

After parsing, expand ? to explicit modes and store only explicit modes.

---

6) Planned ops: executable only

pub enum Slot {
    Var(VarId),
    Const(ConstId),
}

pub enum OpPlan {
    Lookup { pred: PredId, mode: ModeId, args: Box<[Slot]> },
    Not    { pred: PredId, args: Box<[Slot]> },
    Unify  { a: TermTyped, b: TermTyped },
    Compare { op: CmpOp, a: TermTyped, b: TermTyped },
    ArithBind { out: VarId, expr: ArithExpr },
    Aggregate { out: VarId, agg: AggKind, inner: SubPlan },
    ChooseTopK { site: ChooseSiteId, tag: Symbol, k: Slot, group: Slot, score: VarId, item: VarId, inner: SubPlan },
    WitnessPath { site: WitnessSiteId, graph: Slot, from: Slot, to: Slot, out: VarId },
    PathHop { path: Slot, seq: VarId, from: VarId, to: VarId, kind: VarId, evidence: VarId },
}

The engine never runs mode logic; it executes this plan directly.

---

7) Host traits (rust-analyzer adapter lives in raql-host-ra)

pub trait HostTypes {
    type Def: Copy + Eq + std::hash::Hash + std::fmt::Debug;
    type Span: Copy + Eq + std::hash::Hash + std::fmt::Debug;
    type TypeRef: Copy + Eq + std::hash::Hash + std::fmt::Debug;
    type Node: Copy + Eq + std::hash::Hash + std::fmt::Debug;
    type Call: Copy + Eq + std::hash::Hash + std::fmt::Debug;
    type Ref: Copy + Eq + std::hash::Hash + std::fmt::Debug;
    type Impl: Copy + Eq + std::hash::Hash + std::fmt::Debug;
}

pub struct SpanKey {
    pub rel_path: Symbol,
    pub l0: i64,
    pub c0: i64,
    pub l1: i64,
    pub c1: i64,
}

pub trait HostStableKeys: HostTypes {
    fn def_handle(&mut self, d: Self::Def) -> Symbol;
    fn span_key(&mut self, s: Self::Span) -> SpanKey;
    fn typeref_id(&mut self, tr: Self::TypeRef) -> Symbol;
    fn node_id(&mut self, n: Self::Node) -> Symbol;
    fn call_id(&mut self, c: Self::Call) -> Symbol;
    fn ref_id(&mut self, r: Self::Ref) -> Symbol;
    fn impl_id(&mut self, i: Self::Impl) -> Symbol;
    fn world_stamp(&mut self) -> Symbol;
}

For v0.1, prefer a typed extern trait over stringly dispatch. The engine can
translate from RAQL predicates to these methods once at compile time.

---

8) raql-host-ra mappings (rust-analyzer types)

Recommended concrete types:

* Span = rust-analyzer span::Span
* Node = (hir_expand::HirFileId, syntax::SyntaxNodePtr)
* Def  = small enum wrapping the HIR id variants you need
* TypeRef = host-interned handle keyed by hir_ty::Ty

The host must cache stable keys aggressively. The engine assumes these methods
are deterministic within a single analysis snapshot.
